{"step_index":131,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:01:42Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T17:01:42+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T17:01:42+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity_handoff.py`\nTotal Lines: 348\nTotal Bytes: 15551\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python\n2: \"\"\"tools/antigravity_handoff.py — run the prover benchmark through Antigravity.\n3: \n4: Antigravity's `/teamwork-preview` is a slash command inside its IDE, not an API,\n5: so the integration is a file handoff: export the challenges, run the team over\n6: them there, drop what comes back into a directory, verify it here.\n7: \n8: The verification deliberately reuses the *same* path as the seven-model\n9: campaign — `LeanSubprocessProver._run_lean(..., audit_axioms=True)` over a\n10: challenge file whose `prove`/`refute` declarations are two directions of one\n11: `Candidate` — so the result is directly comparable to that baseline rather than\n12: being a differently-scored number.\n13: \n14: Why that matters here specifically: every formalization bug this repository has\n15: found produced an *apparent success*. A model \"proved\" three items that were\n16: `Fin 0` artefacts; another exploited `minCard`'s 0 fallback on an undefined\n17: invariant. A stronger agent team is more likely to find such holes, not less, so\n18: nothing is counted as resolved unless the kernel accepts it under an axiom\n19: audit, and `--strict` additionally re-checks that the accepted direction agrees\n20: with the ground-truth label the benchmark carries.\n21: \n22: Usage:\n23:     python tools/antigravity_handoff.py export --partition gold --out handoff/\n24:     # ... run /teamwork-preview over handoff/, save results into handoff/solved/\n25:     python tools/antigravity_handoff.py verify --partition gold --dir handoff/solved\n26: \"\"\"\n27: from __future__ import annotations\n28: \n29: import argparse\n30: import collections\n31: import json\n32: import os\n33: import re\n34: import sys\n35: \n36: sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))\n37: \n38: from config import CONFIG  # noqa: E402\n39: \n40: BRIEF = \"\"\"\\\n41: # AutoGraphForge — prover benchmark handoff\n42: \n43: Each `Challenge_<id>.lean` states one conjecture once, as `Candidate`, and asks\n44: for **either** direction:\n45: \n46:     theorem prove_<id>  :   Candidate := by sorry\n47:     theorem refute_<id> : ¬ Candidate := by sorry\n48: \n49: Close exactly one, editing the file in place and keeping its name. Leave the\n50: other declaration untouched, `sorry` and all — the verifier removes it.\n51: \n52: What makes a result count:\n53: \n54: * Nothing above the first `theorem` may change: imports, options, `Candidate`.\n55:   Helper lemmas go after `Candidate`, as top-level `theorem`/`lemma`/`def`.\n56: * The chosen theorem keeps its exact name and type. The verifier re-checks the\n57:   type by elaborating `_root_.prove_<id> : _root_.Candidate` itself.\n58: * No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide`, `namespace`, `section`,\n59:   `variable`, custom `notation`/`macro`/`syntax`, or metaprogramming; only\n60:   `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` may appear among the axioms.\n61: * Never run `lake` in this project — it deletes Mathlib.\n62: \n63: `decide` evaluates the invariants on an explicit small graph\n64: (`GraphCalc.ofEdges n [(0, 1), ...]`), so a refutation is usually a witness plus\n65: `decide`. Ground truth is withheld. {n} items in this partition.\n66: \"\"\"\n67: \n68: \n69: def _index(bench: str, partition: str):\n70:     path = os.path.join(bench, f\"challenges_{partition}\", \"index.json\")\n71:     if not os.path.exists(path):\n72:         raise SystemExit(f\"no challenge index at {path} — run \"\n73:                          f\"tools/prover_eval/challenge.py --partition {partition}\")\n74:     return json.load(open(path)), os.path.dirname(path)\n75: \n76: \n77: def do_export(args) -> int:\n78:     index, src = _index(args.benchmark, args.partition)\n79:     os.makedirs(args.out, exist_ok=True)\n80:     os.makedirs(os.path.join(args.out, \"solved\"), exist_ok=True)\n81:     import shutil\n82:     for item in index:\n83:         shutil.copy(os.path.join(src, item[\"file\"]), os.path.join(args.out, item[\"file\"]))\n84:     with open(os.path.join(args.out, \"README.md\"), \"w\") as fh:\n85:         fh.write(BRIEF.format(n=len(index)))\n86:     # The labels stay on this side of the handoff.\n87:     with open(os.path.join(args.out, \".ground_truth.json\"), \"w\") as fh:\n88:         json.dump({i[\"id\"]: {\"label\": i[\"label\"], \"witness_g6\": i.get(\"witness_g6\"),\n89:                              \"statement\": i[\"statement\"]} for i in index}, fh, indent=1)\n90:     print(f\"exported {len(index)} challenges → {args.out}\")\n91:     print(f\"  brief:       {os.path.join(args.out, 'README.md')}\")\n92:     print(f\"  put results in: {os.path.join(args.out, 'solved')}\")\n93:     return 0\n94: \n95: \n96: def _candidate_of(text: str):\n97:     \"\"\"The `abbrev Candidate : Prop := …` body, normalised for comparison.\"\"\"\n98:     m = re.search(r\"abbrev\\s+Candidate\\s*:\\s*Prop\\s*:=(.*?)(?=\\n\\ntheorem )\", text, re.S)\n99:     return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", m.group(1)).strip() if m else None\n100: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
