of vertices, it follows that `k <= n` is always true.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating the total domination implications**\n\nHypothesized that there exists a vertex `v` within any total dominating set `S` of size `k` such that all other vertices are within distance `k` from `v`. This means `ballWithin G k v = univ`.\n\nAnalyzed what `ballWithin G k v = univ` implies, finding it means every vertex is at most distance `k` from `v`.  Recalled that radius is less than or equal to `k`. Recognized that showing `eccentricity G v0 <= k` for some `v0` proves `radius G <= k`.\n\nRealized there's circular reasoning if relying on the center having eccentricity less than or equal to `k`, since the goal is to prove `radius <= k`. Need to directly prove `radius <= k`. Therefore, the eccentricity must be proven for some `v`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\n\ndef test():\n    for n in range(2, 9):\n        for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n            if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\n                nodes = list(G.nodes())\n                # Find all minimum total dominating sets\n                # first find tdn\n                min_tds_list = []\n                for k in range(1, n + 1):\n                    for S in itertools.combinations(nodes, k):\n                        S_set = set(S)\n                        if all(any(u in S_set for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                            min_tds_list.append(S_set)\n                    if min_tds_list:\n                        break\n                # For each minimum TDS S:\n                for S in min_tds_list:\n                    k = len(S)\n                    # Is there a vertex in S with eccentricity <= k?\n                    eccs = [nx.eccentricity(G, v) for v in S]\n                    if not any(e <= k for e in